# Per-element subscope call — the functie-route (besluit 1-A, 2026-08-24)

The tutorial's 2-4 shape: a subscope call *per list element*
(`map each g among … to (output of … with {…}).field`). Besluit 1-A lowers a
PURE-FUNCTION callee to a FunctionDef (row-10 machinery) and the map body to
`MapList(list, λg. Invoke(callee, …))` — no instance, no creation key; the
per-element identity is the list position (clingo's `lelem` index reification).

`Kamer` is a pure function here (one output, a plain total base, an ADDITIVE
body, no own creation, no non-input reads), so `(Kamer of {grondslag=g}).bedrag`
becomes `Invoke(Kamer, g)`. The map result is folded to a SCALAR — the covered,
triple-green form (a list-STORED output attribute has no clingo image; an
additive body stays inside clingo's closed-body +/- fence, S15). Own-authored,
rights-free.

```catala
declaration scope Kamer:
  input grondslag content integer
  output bedrag content integer

scope Kamer:
  definition bedrag equals grondslag + 100

declaration scope Aanslag:
  input grondslagen content list of integer
  output totaal content integer

scope Aanslag:
  definition totaal equals
    combine all b
      among (map each g among grondslagen to (output of Kamer with { -- grondslag: g }).bedrag)
      in acc initially 0 with (acc + b)
```
